            "review_title": "Review at Nam Pla Thai Food",
            "review_text": "Tarraq\nOdense, Denmark1 contribution\n2\nQuirky and exciting interior, but the food doesn’t quite follow through.\nApr 2019 • Friends\nAs in several Vietnamese restaurant, this isn’t on ground floor, but rather on third, and to get to the elevators you have to go through another café (RuNam).\nWhen the elevator door opens you are met with a explosion of color and a nice airconditioned restaurant.\n\nWe were met with friendly and young personnel, though lacking English skills, were able to understand and accommodate us. Sometimes they seemed a little preoccupied with their cell phones, considering this place to be in the more high end of dining.\n\nWe ordered several dishes from the menu, as well as cocktails, fruits juices and soft drinks.\nThe serving of all our 7 participants had a timespan over almost 35 minutes, so the first dish served was cold before the last one was served.\n\nThe presentation of the food was beautiful, with a terroir “back to nature” impression with weed baskets and banana leaves. The scents gave of a wonderful sense when first served, but the presentational awe dimmed over the several minutes of serving.\n\nThe food was somewhat Thai food, but with a Vietnamese sense to it as well. I would rather call it a Thai-Vietnamese-fusion, rather than Thai-cuisine, witch I also find quite intriguing.\n\nThe food was ok, but considering the price tag in comparison to other restaurants in the same price range, it didn’t quite live up to the hyped up image it seemed wanting to be a part of.\n\nThe general patronage of the restaurant was guests in the younger age-range, very styled considering it to be a Monday evening, dressed to impress with expensive labels. All though ordering food and drinks, they seemed more occupied by the selfieperfect surroundigs that would give you an insta-moment of color-gasm.\n\nCome to this place for the perfect photo opportunity and somewhat bland food and drinks, considering the bill.\nRead more\nWritten April 15, 2019",
