            "review_title": "Review at Nam Pla Thai Food",
            "review_text": "Charlesquil\nDublin, California305 contributions\n0\nBest Thai Food in Saigon\nNov 2018 • Couples\nI usually visit this building addressed at 40-42 Phan Boi Chau, District 1 (opposite East Gate, Ben Thanh Market) for cafe RuNam on the ground floor and get a haircut at 4Rau Barber Shop on the 6th Floor. Recently just came to know about Nam Pla Thai Food Restaurant on the 3rd Floor in the same building.\nI came with my wife and we order bấuc Thai dishes like Som Tom, Tom Yum, Roastwd Pork, and Fried Rice. All are very tasty and well presented. I love the som tom placed in a pot with a large banana leave underneath and fried rice served in Lotus leave.\nThe restaurant decoration is also quite unique compare to Thai restaurant as a whole, not only in Vietnam. More to mention, heard that this restaurant belongs to ine of the most famous designers in Vietnam.\nFinally, the price is ok. I recommend for those who like Thai food qnd looking for a good place to eat in Saigon.\nRead more\nWritten November 3, 2018",
